Planet textures
===============

Planet surface and cloud textures: Solar System Scope (INOVE), https://www.solarsystemscope.com/textures/
Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Files (2k, as downloaded 2026-10-03 from https://www.solarsystemscope.com/textures/download/<file>;
sha256 pins in data/planets/SHA256SUMS):
  2k_mercury.jpg  2k_venus_atmosphere.jpg  2k_earth_daymap.jpg  2k_earth_clouds.jpg  2k_moon.jpg
  2k_mars.jpg  2k_jupiter.jpg  2k_saturn.jpg  2k_uranus.jpg  2k_neptune.jpg

Changes made: none to the files. The game rescales each texture's brightness at render time so its
disc-integrated albedo equals the body's measured V-band geometric albedo (Mallama et al. 2017), and
composites Earth's cloud map over its day map; the brightness you see is the data's, the pattern and
colour are the texture's.

Source notes (Solar System Scope): the textures are based on NASA elevation and imagery data, with
colours tuned to true-colour spacecraft and Hubble images; unmapped regions are filled with fictional
terrain matching the surroundings, and colours are slightly more saturated than true colour.

In-game credit line:
  Planet textures: Solar System Scope (solarsystemscope.com), CC BY 4.0

Moon surface mosaics (added 2026-10-11)
======================================
NASA spacecraft imagery, assembled and served by USGS Astrogeology Science Center;
public domain (USGS products' access constraints), with attribution retained.
Triton colour mosaic: NASA/JPL/USGS, Dr. Paul Schenk / Lunar and Planetary Institute.
Exact per-file WMS source URLs: data/planets/SOURCES. Exact downloaded-file SHA256:
data/planets/SHA256SUMS. Files are unmodified service-rendered JPEGs, Callisto at
2048 x 1024 and other moons at 1024 x 512; no fabricated terrain or borrowed maps.
Request extent -180..180 east longitude, -90..90 planetocentric latitude, north up,
EPSG:4326 as exposed by the planetary service: this matches the shader's
u=0.5+east_longitude/360, v=0.5-latitude/180. The service supplies the requested east-longitude -180..180 extent; source
longitude conventions vary by mosaic. We do not assert sub-pixel geodetic precision.

Callisto: Galileo SSI + Voyager global mosaic, monochrome; source selection
resolution varies from ~400 m to ~60 km/pixel gap-fill. Black polar coverage gaps
and mosaic seams remain as in the source; they do not represent dark terrain.
https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/callisto_galileo_voyager_global_mosaic_1km
Io: Galileo SSI/Voyager merged colour mosaic, enhanced/filter-composite colour;
the eye-visible colours are more muted, and surface activity changed between
Voyager and Galileo epochs. We preserve the source composite and disclose it.
https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/io_galileo_ssi_voyager_color_merged_global_mosaic_1km
Europa: Voyager/Galileo SSI 500 m mosaic, monochrome, mixed camera filters.
https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/europa_voyager_galileo_ssi_global_mosaic_500m
Ganymede: Voyager/Galileo SSI global mosaic, monochrome service layer.
https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/ganymede_voyager_galileo_ssi_global_mosaic_1km
Mimas, Enceladus, Tethys, Dione, Rhea: Cassini/Voyager visible-light monochrome
service mosaics, mixed image resolutions and residual lighting/seams.
https://planetarymaps.usgs.gov/ (each per-body layer named in SOURCES)
Triton: Voyager 2 colour mosaic, orange/violet/UV mapped to RGB; enhanced colour,
large unmapped north-polar region and repaired source grid lines, not a complete
natural-colour map of the entire surface.
https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/triton_voyager_2_global_color_mosaic_600m

Not textured: Titan. Available global surface maps are radar/near-IR views
through an opaque visible-light haze. They are not presented as the naked-eye
surface; a dedicated validated visible-light atmosphere remains follow-up work.
All moons use the existing normalized albedo shader; the sim's p_V and Minnaert
k still determine integrated brightness. The maps provide surface pattern only.

Additional in-game credit line:
  Moon mosaics: NASA / USGS; Triton: NASA/JPL, P. Schenk/LPI (public domain; enhanced Io/Triton colour)
